 "_licence": "ODbL 1.0, \u00a9 OpenStreetMap contributors",
 "_why": "Real natural=coastline geometry around the mouth of the Ria de Villaviciosa, captured for the Selorio report, 2026-08-15. It reproduces property 125's stored verdict exactly (4173.8 m, bearing 16.5), so the test measures the same thing production did. Overpass is the app's source; it was unreachable on the capture date, and a test must not reach either one anyway (tests/network_guard.py).",
 "_geography": "The six ways close ACROSS the mouth rather than following the ria inland: their southernmost node is 43.5305789, while the Ria de Villaviciosa water multipolygon (OSM relation 2166590, natural=water/water=river/tidal=yes) reaches 43.4838 -- 7.13 km further in. Measured the same way for the rias of Aviles, Navia and the Nalon estuary: 4.60, 4.90 and 4.37/7.29 km. So the nearest coastline to an inland plot is the mouth, i.e. open sea, and none of the coastline ways in any of those four bboxes carries a name.",
